### Brain read API scenario (VS Code REST Client or Rider HTTP Client). Run top to bottom.
### Fill the seed account values from user-secrets: Seed:SahipEmail / Seed:SahipPassword
### (and Seed:AsistanEmail / Seed:AsistanPassword for the 403 example). Do not commit real values.
### The brain must be configured (README, "Brain"); otherwise every request below answers 503.

@host = http://localhost:5051
@sahipEmail = <Seed:SahipEmail>
@sahipSifre = <Seed:SahipPassword>
@asistanEmail = <Seed:AsistanEmail>
@asistanSifre = <Seed:AsistanPassword>

### 1. Log in as Sahip
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/hesap/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{sahipEmail}}", "password": "{{sahipSifre}}" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2. Status: connected?, vault folder name, waiting and failed captures
GET {{host}}/api/beyin/durum
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Projects (hidden ones are left out), then one project
GET {{host}}/api/beyin/projeler
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/beyin/projeler/kitap-kulubu
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. A day's plan (yyyy-MM-dd). The first read of a day gives its plan lines permanent ids in the plan file.
GET {{host}}/api/beyin/gunler/2026-11-03
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Search (q is required, at most 200 characters; limit 1-50, default 10)
GET {{host}}/api/beyin/ara?q=kitap&limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/beyin/ara?q=takvim&proje=kitap-kulubu
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. One note
GET {{host}}/api/beyin/not?yol=projects/kitap-kulubu/notlar/takvim-kutuphanesi.md
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Refused: bad path -> 400 { errors: { yol: [...] } }
GET {{host}}/api/beyin/not?yol=../kisisel/gizli-not.md
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. A hidden note looks like a missing one -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/beyin/not?yol=kisisel/gizli-not.md
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Refused: empty query -> 400 { errors: { q: [...] } }
GET {{host}}/api/beyin/ara?q=
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9a. Repository bridge (K2.5). The Sahip links a project to owner/repo (the project must exist in the brain) -> 200
PUT {{host}}/api/yonetim/proje-repolari/kitap-kulubu
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "depo": "emre/kitap-kulubu" }

### 9b. All links (Sahip only), then the repository card of a project (beyin.oku): link, last 5 commits, open PR count.
### With no GitHub:Token on the server only the link comes back (durum: tokenYok). 404 when the project has no link.
GET {{host}}/api/yonetim/proje-repolari
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/beyin/projeler/kitap-kulubu/repo
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9c. Remove the link -> 204
DELETE {{host}}/api/yonetim/proje-repolari/kitap-kulubu
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9d. Pick lists for the hand placement of an inbox card (gelen.oku): tag dictionary and folders
GET {{host}}/api/gelen/etiketler
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/gelen/klasorler
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Assistant without the beyin.oku permission -> 403
# @name asistanLogin
POST {{host}}/api/hesap/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{asistanEmail}}", "password": "{{asistanSifre}}" }

###
GET {{host}}/api/beyin/projeler
Authorization: Bearer {{asistanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
